.TH USB-PROTECTION-AGENT 1 "September 2026" "USB Protection 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
usb-protection-agent \- display notifications for blocked USB devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usb-protection-agent
.SH DESCRIPTION
Watches USBGuard device events in the current user session and displays
notifications with Allow Once and Always Allow actions.
The agent starts via XDG Autostart at login and when the application opens.
Only one agent runs per session. Never run this command as root.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR usb-protection (1),
.BR usbguard (1)
